// Exploring the graph
// Aggregations, filters, and a traversal template over your real collections.

// %% Chapters by graph domain
// Count chapters by graph domain:
FOR d IN chapters
  COLLECT domain = d.graph_domain WITH COUNT INTO n
  SORT n DESC
  RETURN { domain, n }

// %% Findings by status
// Findings by status:
FOR d IN findings
  COLLECT status = d.status WITH COUNT INTO n
  SORT n DESC
  RETURN { status, n }

// %% Top pattern types
// Top chapters pattern types:
FOR d IN chapters
  COLLECT pt = d.pattern_type WITH COUNT INTO n
  SORT n DESC LIMIT 15
  RETURN { pattern: pt, n }

// %% Traversal template
// Traversal template — pick a start doc and walk an edge collection (adjust the edge name to your graph; here: evidence edges from a finding):
FOR start IN findings LIMIT 1
  FOR v IN 1..1 ANY start._id evidence
    RETURN DISTINCT v.label

// %% Note on @at directive
// Note on // @at: — the directive parses today but is a valid-time filter only and a near-no-op on this evergreen corpus;
// it activates fully once engine issue #594 ships the query-wide options.at. Don't rely on it for reproducibility yet.
